<p>Pope Leo XIV used the opening days of his first African tour to highlight peace, coexistence, and the Christian legacy of Saint Augustine, visiting Annaba in Algeria before flying on to Cameroon on April 15. In Annaba, he celebrated Mass at the Basilica of Saint Augustine and praised Algeria’s small Catholic community, framing the stop as both a spiritual return to his Augustinian roots and a call for dialogue across religious and political differences. The trip also unfolded amid two parallel tensions. Algerian media reported two suicide attacks in Blida, southwest of Algiers, though an informed source cited by Dawn said no deaths beyond the bombers had been confirmed and Algerian authorities had not publicly commented. At the same time, President Trump stepped up his public criticism of the pope over Iran and other issues, while Leo answered by reaffirming the Gospel’s call to peacemaking and saying the world needs a message of peace and unity.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/uKXlLBJSQ5_zbTMi6OE2TfE1YzHDm3Sr86NdLLLFhxZ0gzmBis-jEQfDXG2b41xPtGf-brn_5q1yYufbmeDvVfks41pqYf4VN3yI85kwfB0438EBMqzv_VLy7r64A8QjX_Y7_WWK35c7rfmZWqABJC-4ZosV8TONZRVW59P1FLG5EzMXUnosMpGxOP7BQQAKwFOVulIz4QSTV4ucLXrZWVyGtlviLI9J5GS6BuSGYtU' alt='Pope Leo XIV presiding over Holy Mass at the Basilica of Saint Augustine in Annaba, Algeria, on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Cameroon pause: Before Leo arrived in Cameroon, the Unity Alliance, a coalition of separatist groups in the Anglophone region, announced a temporary halt in fighting to allow safer movement for civilians, pilgrims, and officials during the visit.</li><li>Historic stop: Dawn described Leo’s journey as the first papal visit to Algeria, giving national weight to a stop already notable for its association with Saint Augustine.</li><li>Next stops: The Vatican’s 11-day African journey will continue beyond Cameroon to Angola and Equatorial Guinea.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Pope Leo XIV: On the flight to Algeria, Leo said he did not fear the Trump administration or speaking loudly about the Gospel’s message, casting his response to criticism as a matter of religious duty. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991786/pope-walks-in-augustines-footsteps-on-algeria-trip'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said the pope was “toying with a country (Iran) that wants a nuclear weapon” and posted that Iran having a nuclear bomb would be “absolutely unacceptable.”. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991929/trump-doubles-down-in-criticising-pope-leo-over-iran'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1991786/pope-walks-in-augustines-footsteps-on-algeria-trip'>Pope walks in Augustine’s footsteps on Algeria trip</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/video/2026/04/15/in-annaba-pope-leo-xiv-hails-algerias-small-catholic-flock-and-saint-augustine'>In Annaba, Pope Leo XIV hails Algeria’s small Catholic flock and Saint Augustine</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/04/14/world/africa/pope-leo-algeria-africa-visit.html'>With Algeria Visit, Pope Leo Returns to His Augustinian Roots</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/africa/638463-pope-leo-begins-cameroon-visit/'>Pope Leo begins Cameroon visit</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/africa/article/3350217/pope-leo-stresses-message-peace-and-unity-despite-another-trump-attack'>Pope Leo stresses message of peace and unity despite another Trump attack</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/pope-leo-attacked-again-by-trump-flies-to-cameroon-on-africa-tour'>Pope Leo, attacked again by Trump, says world needs message of peace</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/pope-doubles-message-peace-unity-trumps-criticism-continues-132061504'>Pope doubles down on message of peace and unity as Trump&#x27;s criticism continues</a> - a